  "notes": "A する verb. Describes a liquid turning opaque and whitish. Commonly encountered in food descriptions (especially ramen and hot pot) and when describing hot springs.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {白濁|はくだく}したスープ (cloudy white soup)\n- {白濁|はくだく}した{湯|ゆ} (milky hot spring water)\n- {白濁|はくだく}{色|いろ} (milky white color)\n\nIn medical contexts, {白濁|はくだく} can describe cloudy urine or other bodily fluids, where it may indicate a health concern.",
